  (text "OpenMUPP v1 pin-header adapter (adapter ID slot 5, R1 = 10k 1 %)\nTargets: CH32V one-wire and two-wire, SWD on hobby boards, STM8 SWIM.\n\nJ1 plugs directly onto J4 of the OpenMUPP v1 probe. Pin numbers of J1 are the J4 pin numbers.\nJ4 pin 19 (VPP) and pin 2 (reserved) stay open. J4 pin 16 (adapter ID) never goes to the target.\nConnect only one target connector (J2, J3 or J4) at a time.\nJ2: no standard exists. The order is the plan proposal (VTREF, GND, SWDIO, SWCLK, NRST, SWO).\nJ3: check the ST SWIM order (VDD, SWIM, GND, NRST) against ST UM1075 before layout.\nJ4: WCH-LinkE layout. Pin 8 (3V3) connects to VTREF. Pin 10 (5V) stays open.\n     Check the GND, 3V3 and 5V positions on a real WCH-LinkE before layout.\nThe CH32 one-wire interface needs no pull-up here: the probe has 2.2k on J4 pin 4.\nJ5 debug UART: labels are from the probe side (RX = probe input)."
    (at 30.48 40.64 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "30b48da6-1448-4302-9b62-e75b872292e1")
  )
